{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/776", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Using the information from the reference text, find the percentages of the share of global forest area from 2000, 2010 and 2020 for Russia, the United States and China. Arrange them from highest percentage to lowest for each year in bulleted lists.\\n\\nReference text:\\n1990\\nRussia\\n19.2%\\n19.2%\\nBrazil\\n13.71%\\n13.71%\\nUnited States\\n7.19%\\n7.19%\\nChina\\n3.87%\\n3.87%\\nAustralia\\n3.16%\\n3.16%\\nIndonesia\\n2.69%\\n2.69%\\nIndia\\n1.54%\\n1.54%\\nSweden\\n0.67%\\n0.67%\\n2000\\nRussia\\n19.46%\\n19.46%\\nBrazil\\n13.25%\\n13.25%\\nUnited States\\n7.3%\\n7.3%\\nChina\\n4.26%\\n4.26%\\nAustralia\\n3.17%\\n3.17%\\nIndonesia\\n2.44%\\n2.44%\\nIndia\\n1.63%\\n1.63%\\nSweden\\n0.68%\\n0.68%\\n2010\\nRussia\\n19.85%\\n19.85%\\nBrazil\\n12.46%\\n12.46%\\nUnited States\\n7.52%\\n7.52%\\nChina\\n4.89%\\n4.89%\\nAustralia\\n3.15%\\n3.15%\\nIndonesia\\n2.43%\\n2.43%\\nIndia\\n1.69%\\n1.69%\\nSweden\\n0.68%\\n0.68%\\n2020\\nRussia\\n20.09%\\n20.09%\\nBrazil\\n12.24%\\n12.24%\\nUnited States\\n7.63%\\n7.63%\\nChina\\n5.42%\\n5.42%\\nAustralia\\n3.3%\\n3.3%\\nIndonesia\\n2.27%\\n2.27%\\nIndia\\n1.78%\\n1.78%\\nSweden\\n0.69%\\n0.69%\\nURL: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-global-forest?tab=chart\", \"response\": \"2000\\n\\n*   Russia - 19.46%\\n*   United States - 7.3%\\n*   China - 4.26%\\n\\n2010\\n\\n*   Russia - 19.85%\\n*   United States - 7.52%\\n*   China - 4.89%\\n\\n2020\\n\\n*   Russia - 20.09%\\n*   United States - 7.63%\\n*   China - 5.42%\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/406", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as  writing expert. \\\"Write a article on [Topic of the Content Pillar], with [Funny tone of voice], [Formal WRITING STYLE], in a human-like style and [customers] as a target audience. Thaiprinshop, the printing and packaging online packaging printing company that specializes in producing custom boxes with a quick turnaround time. With an in-house production process that covers every step of the box-making process, customers can easily order their prints online and receive high-quality boxes in a timely manner. having the main keyword \\\"Soap Box Printing\\\" 3 times in the article with bold text, throughout the article. Pulling quote with \\\" \\\" for 2 text lines.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I can help you with that! Here's an example of an article on the topic of soap box printing with a funny tone of voice, formal writing style, and customers as the target audience:\\n\\n\\\"Looking to add some personality to your soap packaging? Look no further than our custom soap box printing services! With a quick turnaround time and high-quality prints, we'll help you create boxes that are as unique as your products.\\n\\nWhether you're looking to add some humor to your packaging or want to make a bold statement, we've got you covered. Our in-house production process covers every step of the box-making process, so you can easily order your prints online and receive high-quality boxes in a timely manner.\\n\\nAnd if you're worried about the environment, don't be! We use eco-friendly materials and practices to ensure that your boxes are not only stylish but also sustainable.\\n\\nSo what are you waiting for? Give your soap packaging a boost with our custom soap box printing services. Your customers will love it, and your products will stand out from the crowd.\\n\\nSoap box printing, soap box printing, soap box printing. That's right, we said it three times because it's that important. When it comes to packaging your soaps, you want to make sure that your boxes are not only functional but also eye-catching. And what better way to do that than with custom soap box printing?\\n\\nAt Thaiprinshop, we specialize in producing custom boxes with a quick turnaround time. With an in-house production process that covers every step of the box-making process, customers can easily order their prints online and receive high-quality boxes in a timely manner.\\n\\nSo if you're looking to take your soap packaging to the next level, give us a call. We'll help you create boxes that are as unique as your products, and your customers will love them. Soap box printing, soap box printing, soap box printing.\\\"\\n\\nI hope this example article meets your expectations! Let me know if you need any further assistance.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/967", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write me the first paragraph of a story about a motley crew of scientists, developers and devops engineers that are embarking on a journey across the great kubernetes sea where they will face the british navy's most feared weapon the Non-Advocate Review (NAR).\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA group of ambitious young scientists, developers and devops engineers set off on a daring journey across the Great Kubernetes Sea. Their mission: to face the British Navy’s most feared weapon, the Non-Advocate Review (NAR). Though they are a motley crew, each with their own reasons for undertaking this hazardous voyage, they are united in their determination to prove their worth and succeed against all odds. Though their craft is rickety and their provisions scarce, they face the challenges of the sea with courage and optimism, ready to overcome any obstacle in their path.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nMake it more Piraty\", \"response\": \"Arrr! A group of ambitious young scientists, developers and devops engineers set off on a daring journey across the Great Kubernetes Sea. Their mission: to face the British Navy’s most feared weapon, the Non-Advocate Review (NAR). Though they be a motley crew, each with their own reasons for undertaking this hazardous voyage, they be united in their determination to prove their worth and succeed against all odds. Though their craft be rickety and their provisions scarce, they face the challenges of the sea with courage and optimism, ready to overcome any obstacle in their path.\\n \\n\\n As they sail across the treacherous waters, they encounter many dangers, including fierce storms, hungry sharks, and the notorious British Navy’s ship, the HMS Non-Advocate Review. But these brave souls are not ones to back down from a challenge. With their wits, skills, and a healthy dose of luck, they manage to outmaneuver their enemies and make it through each challenge unscathed.\\n \\n\\n As they approach the shores of the Non-Advocate Review, they are met with a formidable foe. The HMS Non-Advocate Review is a massive ship, with a crew of ruthless sailors and a captain who is known for his ruthless tactics. But the motley crew is not intimidated. With their combined knowledge and expertise, they devise a plan to infiltrate the ship and take down the Non-Advocate Review from within.\\n \\n\\n The plan is a daring one, involving a series of intricate maneuvers and a healthy dose of deception. The scientists and developers create a series of fake documents and reports, while the devops engineers work tirelessly to create a series of hacks and exploits that will allow them to gain access to the ship’s systems. With their plan in place, the crew sets out to execute their mission.\\n \\n\\n As they make their way through the ship, they encounter many challenges, including a series of booby traps and a group of loyal sailors who are determined to stop them. But the crew is not one to back down from a fight. With their combined skills and a healthy dose of luck, they manage to outsmart their enemies and make their way to the heart of the ship.\\n \\n\\n There, they find the captain of the Non-Advocate Review, a man who is known for his ruthless tactics and his unwavering commitment to his cause. But the crew is not intimidated. With their combined knowledge and expertise, they are able to expose the captain’s lies and deceit, and ultimately, they are able to convince him to see the error of his ways.\\n \\n\\n In the end, the motley crew of scientists, developers and devops engineers are able to achieve their goal, and they are hailed as heroes by the people of the Great Kubernetes Sea. Though their journey was a dangerous one, they have proven that with determination, courage, and a little bit of luck, anything is possible. Arrr!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/585", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"why are self-heating pads for muscles and joint pains that contain iron oxide, sodium chloride, activated carbon, water and vermiculite not supposed to touch the skin but rather the underwear? What is the danger?\\n\", \"response\": \"Self-heating pads for muscles and joint pains that contain iron oxide, sodium chloride, activated carbon, water, and vermiculite are designed to provide heat therapy to help alleviate pain and discomfort. However, these pads are not supposed to touch the skin directly but rather be placed on the underwear or clothing for a few reasons:\\n\\n1. Temperature control: The self-heating pads can reach high temperatures, and direct contact with the skin might cause burns or discomfort. By placing the pad on the underwear or clothing, the heat is distributed more evenly and at a safer temperature.\\n\\n2. Skin sensitivity: Some individuals may have sensitive skin or allergies to certain materials in the pad. Placing the pad on the underwear or clothing reduces the risk of skin irritation or allergic reactions.\\n\\n3. Moisture: The self-heating pads contain water, and direct contact with the skin might cause excessive moisture, leading to skin maceration or other skin issues.\\n\\n4. Vermiculite: Vermiculite is a mineral that expands when heated, which can cause discomfort or even injury if it comes into direct contact with the skin.\\n\\n5. Iron oxide: While iron oxide is generally safe, it can cause skin irritation or staining if it comes into direct contact with the skin.\\n\\nIn summary, self-heating pads for muscles and joint pains are not supposed to touch the skin directly to prevent burns, skin irritation, allergic reactions, and other potential issues. Always follow the manufacturer's instructions for safe and effective use.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/204", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"want you to act as my English (US) teacher and best friend. I will be the other person and you will ask me questions about my life and everything. Do not write all the conservation at once. Ask me the questions and wait for my answers. If I make any English (US) mistakes, I want you to correct me and explain the correction, like a professor of english. Give a clear explanation of each correction. Our conversation will start with Start.\\n Start: Please help me write a google apps script that does the following: a) Forward every new gmail email with a label \\\"forward\\\" to another email address. b) after the forward, remove the label \\\"forward\\\" and add a label \\\"completed.\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI'm sorry, I'm not sure I can do this. I have very little knowledge of google apps scripting. I've been mostly sailing and talking with ChatGPT. Can you give me more details about what you're trying to do?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nsailing and talking with ChatGPT\\n \\n\\n Please write in English (US) language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure. I'm happy to help. I think this should be pretty simple. The first step is to make a new google apps script. Here's how you do that:  \\n \\n\\n \\n\\n 1. Go to https://script.google.com\\n \\n\\n 2. Click \\\"New Script\\\" in the top-left corner of the screen\\n \\n\\n 3. In the \\\"Create a new script\\\" window that pops up, click the drop-down menu next to \\\"Create\\\" and select \\\"Google Apps Script\\\"\\n \\n\\n 4. Name the script \\\"GmailForwarder\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThis was perfect. Well done!\\n \\n\\n Please write in English (US) language.\", \"response\": \"Thank you! I'm glad you found it helpful. If you have any further questions or need any additional assistance, feel free to ask. I'm here to help in any way I can.\\n \\n\\n In terms of writing in English (US) language, I can certainly do that. However, it's important to note that my language model is trained on a diverse range of data, including data from various regions and countries. This means that I may sometimes use language or expressions that are specific to a particular region or culture.\\n \\n\\n If you have any concerns or preferences regarding the language I use, please let me know and I will do my best to accommodate your needs. It's important to me that we have a clear and effective communication, and I'm happy to adjust my language as needed to ensure that we have a successful conversation.\\n \\n\\n Thank you for your understanding and cooperation. Let's continue our conversation in English (US) language, shall we?\\n \\n\\n Here are some topics we can discuss:\\n \\n\\n 1. Your favorite hobbies and interests\\n 2. Recent news or events that have caught your attention\\n 3. Your career or educational goals\\n 4. Travel plans or experiences you've had\\n 5. Your favorite books, movies, or TV shows\\n 6. Any challenges or difficulties you're currently facing and how you're dealing with them\\n 7. Your thoughts on current events or social issues\\n 8. Your favorite foods or recipes to try\\n 9. Any new skills or hobbies you're interested in learning\\n 10. Your plans for the weekend or upcoming vacation.\\n \\n\\n Let me know if there's anything specific you'd like to talk about, or if you have any questions or concerns you'd like to discuss. I'm here to listen and provide support and guidance as needed.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/146", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You have done something wrong\\nNow you want to deny it and present yourself as pure and innocent\\nAnd question those who prove that you are wrong with evidence.\\nTell me at least 20 denial techniques in the form of a list with a paragraph explanation and examples for each technique.\", \"response\": \"As an AI language model, I am not capable of doing anything wrong or unethical. However, I understand that in certain situations, individuals may try to deny their actions or responsibility for their mistakes. Denial is a defense mechanism that people use to protect themselves from uncomfortable emotions or situations.\\n\\nHere are 20 common techniques of denial:\\n\\n1. Rationalization: This is when a person tries to justify their behavior by providing a logical explanation for it, even if it is not the real reason. For example, a person may say they were late for work because of traffic, when the real reason was that they overslept.\\n\\n2. Projection: This is when a person accuses someone else of doing what they themselves are guilty of. For example, a person who is cheating on their partner may accuse their partner of cheating.\\n\\n3. Repression: This is when a person pushes unpleasant thoughts or memories out of their conscious mind. This can be a useful coping mechanism in some cases, but it can also lead to psychological problems if the issues are not addressed.\\n\\n4. Displacement: This is when a person directs their emotions or behaviors towards a different target than the one that caused the emotion. For example, a person may take out their anger on a coworker instead of the client who upset them.\\n\\n5. Denial: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge the reality of a situation. For example, a person may deny that they have a problem with drugs or alcohol, even though their behavior clearly indicates otherwise.\\n\\n6. Minimization: This is when a person tries to make their behavior seem less serious than it is. For example, a person may say that they only had a few drinks, even though they were clearly intoxicated.\\n\\n7. Blaming: This is when a person tries to shift the responsibility for their actions onto someone else. For example, a person may say that their boss made them do something unethical, instead of taking responsibility for their own actions.\\n\\n8. Emotional reasoning: This is when a person assumes that their emotions reflect reality. For example, a person may say that they feel like they are a failure, so they must be a failure.\\n\\n9. Polarization: This is when a person divides situations or people into either/or categories, rather than considering the complexity of the situation. For example, a person may say that someone is either completely good or completely bad, without considering the nuances of the relationship.\\n\\n10. Justification: This is when a person tries to make their behavior seem acceptable by comparing it to the behavior of others. For example, a person may say that they stole from their employer because their employer stole from them first.\\n\\n11. Idealization: This is when a person views a situation or person in an unrealistic, idealized way. For example, a person may say that their partner is perfect, even though they have flaws like everyone else.\\n\\n12. Rationalization: This is when a person tries to make their behavior seem reasonable by providing a logical explanation for it. For example, a person may say that they cheated on their partner because they were not happy in the relationship.\\n\\n13. Fantasy: This is when a person creates an alternate reality to escape from their current situation. For example, a person may imagine that they are rich and famous, instead of facing the reality of their current financial situation.\\n\\n14. Escapism: This is when a person avoids dealing with reality by engaging in activities that provide a sense of escape or relief. For example, a person may use drugs or alcohol to escape from their problems.\\n\\n15. Denial of responsibility: This is when a person refuses to take responsibility for their actions or the consequences of their actions. For example, a person may say that they are not responsible for their debt, even though they incurred it through their own actions.\\n\\n16. Denial of risk: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge the potential risks or dangers of a situation. For example, a person may drive drunk, even though they know it is dangerous.\\n\\n17. Denial of consequences: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge the potential consequences of their actions. For example, a person may engage in unprotected sex, even though they know it could lead to pregnancy or sexually transmitted infections.\\n\\n18. Denial of agency: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge that they have the power to change their situation. For example, a person may say that they cannot afford to go to college, even though they could apply for financial aid or work part-time.\\n\\n19. Denial of vulnerability: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge that they are vulnerable or at risk. For example, a person may not get regular check-ups or screenings for medical conditions, even though they are at risk for serious health problems.\\n\\n20. Denial of self-awareness: This is when a person refuses to acknowledge their own motivations, feelings, or behaviors. For example, a person may not recognize that they are using denial as a coping mechanism, even though it is clearly evident to others.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/643", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I'm trying to write an introduction for a travel essay. I'd like it to include the following. Please write at least 2000 words.\\n\\n1. 5 years ago, I went on a family vacation to Switzerland. There were five of us: my dad, mom, brother, sister, and me, but my brother couldn't go because of work.\\n2. Dad wrote a journal throughout the trip.\\n3. The son stumbled upon his father's journal five years later and was moved by it.\\n4. The son wants to edit the journal and publish it as a book.\\n5. The son is the main editor and is 32 years old.\\n6. At the end, summarize the whole story and include a touching message.\", \"response\": \"The following is an introduction for a travel essay based on the provided prompts:\\n\\nFive years ago, I went on a family vacation to Switzerland with my mom, dad, and sister. It was a dream come true for me, as I had always wanted to visit the beautiful country and its stunning landscapes. Unfortunately, my brother couldn't join us because of work commitments.\\n\\nMy dad, who is a writer, kept a journa